  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Data Analysis",
    "description": "This project was part of [Computational methods of Data Analysis] course.\n\n1. Music Genre Classification\n- Make 90 samples of 5 seconds of music clips from each music genre or band.\n- Use linear discriminant analysis as a supervised learning algorithm\n- Train the program with 70 samples, test it with 20 samples, cross-validate the program \n- The success rate of classification is 80% \n\n2. Principal Component Analysis \n- With three different videos with different viewpoint angle, find principal component by using Singular Value Decomposition (SVM) \n- Captures the movement in the view in a lower dimension\n\n3. Ultrasound Analysis \n- With given noised data of dog’s stomach, demonstrate understanding in Fourier transform and filter the data to find (x, y, z) location of marble inside of the stomach \n\n",
